WEBVTT

00:34.400 --> 00:36.636
<i>We now return to An Early Draft</i>

00:36.670 --> 00:38.805
<i>of A Streetcar Named Desire.</i>

00:38.840 --> 00:42.544
Deb? Deb!

00:42.578 --> 00:45.615
Debbie!

00:45.650 --> 00:47.017
Good night, Lois.

00:47.051 --> 00:48.719
Sorry about hitting
you at dinner.

00:48.754 --> 00:50.922
It was nice of the manager
not to call the cops.

00:50.956 --> 00:52.323
Yeah, it worked out.

00:52.357 --> 00:53.859
Happy anniversary.

00:55.829 --> 00:57.198
I can't remember if I'm supposed

00:57.232 --> 00:58.933
to sleep on my stomach
or my back.

00:58.967 --> 01:00.936
What does
the current literature say?

01:00.970 --> 01:02.271
Peter, go check
on Stewie.

01:02.306 --> 01:04.407
Fine.

01:04.441 --> 01:06.643
Oh, my God, look at you.

01:06.678 --> 01:07.778
You're out of breath.

01:07.812 --> 01:10.416
It's 15 feet
from your door to mine.

01:10.450 --> 01:11.817
Aw, what's the matter, Stewie?

01:11.851 --> 01:13.220
You a little scared in here?

01:13.254 --> 01:15.022
Don't worry,
there's no monsters.

01:15.057 --> 01:16.490
Of course there's
no monsters.

01:16.525 --> 01:17.960
Or are you worried
about what happened

01:17.994 --> 01:19.560
to that family
down the street?

01:19.595 --> 01:21.931
Those three guys broke in,
beat up the father

01:21.966 --> 01:24.000
with a croquet mallet,
and then stole the baby,

01:24.034 --> 01:26.071
and nobody knows
where the baby is now?

01:26.105 --> 01:27.745
Is that what you're
thinking about, buddy?

01:27.773 --> 01:29.175
I am now!

01:29.209 --> 01:32.044
Tell you what, Daddy'll
read you a bedtime story.

01:32.079 --> 01:33.381
Ah, let's see.

01:33.415 --> 01:35.350
<i>Dr. Seuss, Peter Rabbit...</i>

01:35.384 --> 01:38.421
<i>Ah, here we go,
James Michener's Hawaii.</i>

01:38.456 --> 01:40.657
Let's skip three feet in.

01:40.691 --> 01:42.593
Aah, Pearl Harbor!

01:42.628 --> 01:44.329
Okay, let's see, uh...

01:44.364 --> 01:45.465
Ah, here we go.

01:45.499 --> 01:47.233
<i>Fairy Tales.</i>

01:48.801 --> 01:50.303
Oh, not on your lap.

01:50.337 --> 01:52.973
Aah, gross!

01:53.008 --> 01:54.843
"Jack and the Beanstalk."

01:54.877 --> 01:57.346
Now, that title could be
a fairy tale or a porn.

01:57.381 --> 01:59.383
Let's find out.

02:08.664 --> 02:10.832
Jack, we need to put
food on the table.

02:10.867 --> 02:12.167
Oh, give me a break, Wife.

02:12.201 --> 02:14.003
You know, if you could
spin straw into gold

02:14.038 --> 02:16.240
or-or maybe meth,
I wouldn't need a job.

02:16.274 --> 02:17.641
Well, then, sell the cow!

02:17.676 --> 02:19.677
And be sure you get
real money for it.

02:19.711 --> 02:21.046
What else would I get?

02:21.080 --> 02:23.049
I don't know-- magic beans?

02:23.083 --> 02:24.550
There are magic beans?

02:24.584 --> 02:25.584
I don't know.

02:25.619 --> 02:26.921
Who cares?

02:26.955 --> 02:28.790
Well, what's
magic about them?

02:28.824 --> 02:30.893
Don't get magic
beans, you idiot.

02:30.927 --> 02:32.428
What? I-I'd never
even freaking heard

02:32.462 --> 02:34.098
of magic beans
till you said them.

02:34.132 --> 02:36.600
If I do get them,
it's you what caused it.

02:41.709 --> 02:43.177
So, you're selling me?

02:43.211 --> 02:44.678
Yeah, well, you heard
her back there.

02:44.713 --> 02:48.483
She wants her stupid magic beans
so the whole world has to stop.

02:48.517 --> 02:49.884
Halt, travelers!

02:49.919 --> 02:51.153
Oh, my God!

02:51.189 --> 02:52.522
Why do you look like that?

02:52.557 --> 02:55.193
Ah, all of these stories
were written by Germans.

02:55.227 --> 02:58.163
But nobody can cross my bridge
without paying a toll.

02:58.198 --> 02:59.532
A toll? Like what?

02:59.567 --> 03:01.735
You have to name three
great Jewish athletes

03:01.769 --> 03:04.139
or pay a thousand
gold coins.

03:04.173 --> 03:06.409
Uh, Hank Greenberg,

03:06.443 --> 03:07.910
Sandy Koufax

03:07.945 --> 03:09.947
and, uh, Gal Fridman,

03:09.981 --> 03:11.483
Olympic windsurfer.

03:11.517 --> 03:12.917
Took gold in Athens in 2000

03:12.952 --> 03:14.720
and the bronze
in Atlanta in '96.

03:14.755 --> 03:16.757
I can see you're
on your phone.

03:16.791 --> 03:18.424
Oh, come on,
I'm supposed to go into town

03:18.458 --> 03:19.693
and sell this cow.

03:19.727 --> 03:21.428
Ooh, you're selling that cow?

03:21.462 --> 03:24.533
I don't have much, but I'll give
you some magic beans for it.

03:26.436 --> 03:29.774
That's exactly
what I was supposed to get!

03:30.977 --> 03:33.278
<i>I said not magic beans.</i>

03:33.312 --> 03:35.182
Look, le-let's
just admit we both

03:35.216 --> 03:36.517
kind of got our
wires crossed,

03:36.551 --> 03:38.953
and commit to being
clearer in the future.

03:38.988 --> 03:41.424
Jack, I'm sick of your
irresponsible behavior.

03:41.458 --> 03:43.960
Like when you were supposed
to be babysitting Georgie Porgie

03:43.995 --> 03:46.397
and his sleazy brother
Rick Porgie.

03:46.432 --> 03:49.000
Hey, Rick, you want to kiss
some girls and make them cry?

03:49.034 --> 03:52.439
No, but let's thumb-blast them
and make them puke.

03:52.473 --> 03:54.707
What the hell are we supposed
to do with these anyway?

03:54.742 --> 03:56.977
I knew you'd be mad, so
I've asked the band Heart

03:57.012 --> 03:59.982
to explain these beans in a
way you can dreamily digest.

04:00.017 --> 04:02.285
♪ These beans

04:02.319 --> 04:06.291
♪ Go on when I close my eyes

04:06.325 --> 04:09.328
♪ Every second of the night

04:09.362 --> 04:12.467
♪ I live another life

04:12.501 --> 04:18.106
♪ These beans that sleep
when it's cold outside. ♪

04:18.141 --> 04:21.678
They changed the word
"dreams" to "beans."

04:21.712 --> 04:24.282
I-I was hoping they'd
change a few more words

04:24.317 --> 04:26.084
to pertain to our situation,

04:26.118 --> 04:28.221
but I-I-I'm just
happy they did this.

04:28.255 --> 04:29.590
Jack, this is ridiculous.

04:29.624 --> 04:31.493
Tomorrow I want you
to go back out there

04:31.527 --> 04:34.162
and look for a job
that pays actual money.

04:34.196 --> 04:36.032
These things are worthless.

04:38.135 --> 04:40.304
I know she's gone,
but can you do the other one?

04:40.339 --> 04:42.508
♪ What about beans?

04:42.542 --> 04:46.545
♪ Don't you want someone
to care about you? ♪

05:00.200 --> 05:02.535
"Mary Davis gives birth to...

05:02.569 --> 05:04.538
lamb?"

05:04.572 --> 05:06.574
Holy crap!

05:15.520 --> 05:17.455
Oh, my God!

05:17.490 --> 05:18.924
Wha-What is that?

05:18.958 --> 05:22.361
I think those magic beans
grew into a giant beanstalk.

05:22.396 --> 05:24.077
Hey, where the hell'd
that thing come from?

05:24.098 --> 05:26.601
It's blocking my view of
Little Miss Muffet's tuffet.

05:26.635 --> 05:28.637
Ooh, isn't my tuffet soft

05:28.672 --> 05:30.740
and pink and wonderful?

05:30.775 --> 05:32.376
Ah, damn it!
I need to see that

05:32.411 --> 05:34.078
so I can make curds and whey.

05:34.112 --> 05:35.581
Relax, Rumpleforeskin.

05:35.615 --> 05:38.151
This is a magic beanstalk
that grew overnight.

05:38.185 --> 05:39.519
And I'm gonna climb it.

05:39.553 --> 05:40.888
Jack, what are you
talking about?

05:40.922 --> 05:42.557
You can't climb all
the way up there.

05:42.592 --> 05:43.725
I have to.

05:43.759 --> 05:45.927
My old gym coach is over there
with a whistle.

05:46.963 --> 05:48.665
Come on, Jack,
your brother was

05:48.700 --> 05:50.400
varsity beanstalk climbing.

05:50.435 --> 05:52.436
He's dead!

06:03.987 --> 06:06.657
And now to throw
this handful of change down

06:06.691 --> 06:09.661
because I'm a psychopath.

06:09.695 --> 06:10.962
Aah, damn it!

06:10.997 --> 06:12.899
Thank you!

06:14.636 --> 06:17.037
I say, who the
devil are you? Go away!

06:17.071 --> 06:18.239
Aw, I-I'm sorry.

06:18.273 --> 06:19.874
Are you taking
a goose poop?

06:19.908 --> 06:21.577
I'm not defecating,
you nitwit.

06:21.611 --> 06:22.611
I'm laying an egg.

06:27.352 --> 06:29.354
Golden eggs!

06:29.389 --> 06:30.923
Oh, my God!

06:30.958 --> 06:32.525
This is probably
what famous black rappers

06:32.559 --> 06:35.429
eat for breakfast.

06:35.463 --> 06:37.466
Who goes there?!

06:37.501 --> 06:40.036
Oh, boy.
You woke up dum-dum.

06:41.272 --> 06:44.108
Fee-fi-fo-fum.

06:44.143 --> 06:47.879
I smell the blood
of an English man.

06:47.913 --> 06:50.450
It's odd that you would speak
gibberish of your own choosing

06:50.484 --> 06:52.152
and not make it rhyme.

06:52.186 --> 06:53.721
How did you get here?

06:53.755 --> 06:54.856
By beanstalk.

06:54.891 --> 06:56.191
How did you get up here?

06:56.225 --> 06:58.094
This is just a house
floating in the air.

06:58.128 --> 06:59.696
I fell from a higher cloud.

06:59.730 --> 07:01.800
That is not what happened.
H-He's out of his mind.

07:01.834 --> 07:04.469
He just sits in his room all
day and inhales hair spray.

07:04.503 --> 07:06.807
Well, you can't have my goose.

07:06.841 --> 07:08.942
Okay, two men
fighting over me.

07:08.976 --> 07:10.244
Neat.

07:10.279 --> 07:12.213
All right, we're just gonna
have to quietly run away.

07:12.247 --> 07:13.683
I'll create a diversion.

07:13.718 --> 07:14.983
Aah! Look at me!

07:15.018 --> 07:16.418
Look at me! Look at me!

07:39.319 --> 07:40.686
Damn beanstalk.

07:40.720 --> 07:42.388
Hey, Little Boy Brown!

07:42.423 --> 07:44.024
You said you were
gonna help me saw.

07:44.059 --> 07:45.592
I can't
find no gloves!

08:11.329 --> 08:13.865
Jack six, giant zero.

08:13.900 --> 08:16.368
What? What? Why-why
is that six points?

08:16.402 --> 08:17.869
Oh, Jack, you're safe.

08:17.904 --> 08:19.506
I was so worried.

08:19.541 --> 08:21.041
And I got this golden goose.

08:21.075 --> 08:23.077
Our troubles are over.

08:23.112 --> 08:24.979
Well, our-our money
troubles are over.

08:25.014 --> 08:28.385
Our sexual troubles are still...
are still very much alive.

08:34.929 --> 08:37.698
Now we wait.

08:37.732 --> 08:39.134
"The end."

08:39.168 --> 08:41.102
So, the lesson there is
if you steal,

08:41.137 --> 08:43.105
you better be ready
to murder, too.

08:43.140 --> 08:45.274
What do you say
we read another one?

08:45.309 --> 08:48.212
Wow, you got a great view
into Bonnie's window from here.

08:48.246 --> 08:50.281
Man, how do you get
any work done?

08:50.316 --> 08:52.117
What do you mean?
Lois is prettier than Bonnie.

08:52.152 --> 08:53.419
Oh, I get it.

08:53.453 --> 08:54.820
It's worse, but it's different.

08:54.856 --> 08:55.923
Okay, all right,
so that's something.

08:55.958 --> 08:56.958
Okay.

09:01.348 --> 09:03.584
So I got out of the
car to take a leak,

09:03.619 --> 09:05.286
because I'd been drinking,
and I didn't know

09:05.320 --> 09:06.787
it was next to a
children's park.

09:06.822 --> 09:08.124
But anyway, that's
why this lady

09:08.158 --> 09:10.226
has to watch whenever
I play with you.

09:10.260 --> 09:11.695
Both hands
on the book, please.

09:11.730 --> 09:13.663
It's my son!
Come on!

09:13.697 --> 09:14.665
Geez!

09:14.699 --> 09:16.034
Thank you, Maya.

09:16.068 --> 09:19.739
All right, the next story is
"Little Red Riding Hood."

09:24.213 --> 09:26.315
<i>Red Riding Hood
was choosing her clothes</i>

09:26.349 --> 09:28.685
<i>for a journey
across the forest.</i>

09:28.719 --> 09:29.986
You know, if I had the guts,

09:30.021 --> 09:31.522
I would be
Little White Turtleneck.

09:31.556 --> 09:33.592
And by "guts," I mean "body."

09:33.626 --> 09:37.463
Red, don't forget this basket
of food for Grandma.

09:37.498 --> 09:39.333
This whole thing is
way too heavy.

09:39.367 --> 09:41.469
Wh-why are you putting
a bag of ice in here?

09:41.504 --> 09:44.707
Is this... is this
a Coors Party Ball?

09:44.741 --> 09:45.875
Is Grandma going
to be entertaining

09:45.909 --> 09:47.911
Florida Jet Ski people?

09:47.945 --> 09:50.548
Remember, stay on the path
and you'll be fine.

09:50.582 --> 09:52.785
Oh, yes, great advice
from mother of the year.

09:52.819 --> 09:56.523
You do realize Grandma
lives 68 miles away, right?

09:56.557 --> 09:59.026
You-you're sending your
child out there to die.

10:04.035 --> 10:06.303
♪ Skipping song,
skipping song ♪

10:06.337 --> 10:08.841
♪ No one's here
to call me gay. ♪

10:08.875 --> 10:11.277
If you were my son,
I would kill you.

10:11.311 --> 10:13.946
Really? Because I hear
your son is a sap.

10:15.316 --> 10:16.584
If you're gonna
hit the king,

10:16.618 --> 10:18.619
you better kill the king.

10:28.302 --> 10:29.368
Oh, hey.

10:29.403 --> 10:30.603
You're the wolf, right?

10:30.637 --> 10:32.339
Yup, and don't forget
"big" and "bad."

10:34.009 --> 10:35.176
Nah.

10:38.148 --> 10:41.452
So, um, what happened with you
and those three little pigs?

10:41.487 --> 10:43.353
Wh-Why did you want
to eat them so badly?

10:43.387 --> 10:46.658
It-it's so amazing that that's
what people think happened.

10:46.693 --> 10:48.828
First of all, I didn't want
to eat them, all right?

10:48.863 --> 10:50.230
I wanted to talk
to one of them.

10:50.264 --> 10:51.231
About what?

10:51.265 --> 10:52.467
Well, she was
my ex-girlfriend,

10:52.502 --> 10:55.036
and I believed
I was due an explanation

10:55.071 --> 10:57.340
about why she was
such a  whore.

10:57.374 --> 10:59.176
All right, well, I'm
off to my grandmother's,

10:59.210 --> 11:01.813
but before I go, I better
take a deep-woods dump.

11:01.847 --> 11:04.350
Her bathroom is right
off the dining room.

11:04.384 --> 11:08.155
So, it's either now
or three days from now.

11:11.494 --> 11:12.861
Where are you going, dear?

11:12.896 --> 11:15.264
I got to go check
on my shoe apartment complex.

11:15.298 --> 11:18.035
Old woman breeds
like a gopher.

11:22.142 --> 11:24.177
Hello?
Is anyone home?

11:24.211 --> 11:26.947
Ay, no, no.

11:26.981 --> 11:29.885
I can hear
the muffled Mexican music.

11:31.288 --> 11:32.822
Look, if you guys
don't shape up,

11:32.857 --> 11:33.958
I'm gonna rent this place

11:33.992 --> 11:36.360
to Goldilocks
and the three bears.

11:36.395 --> 11:38.330
Ooh, this is nice.

11:38.364 --> 11:40.968
It's every bit as
darling as you said.

11:41.002 --> 11:42.902
They're gonna
fix up the place.

11:47.977 --> 11:49.412
Who is it?

11:49.446 --> 11:51.380
It's your granddaughter, Red.

11:51.415 --> 11:53.117
How do I know it's you?

11:53.152 --> 11:54.819
Oh, come on, that's
a perfect imitation.

11:54.854 --> 11:58.057
Open up. I brought strawberry
shortcake and Cool Whip.

11:58.091 --> 11:59.059
And what?

11:59.093 --> 12:00.794
Oh, sorry.
I mean Cool Hwhip.

12:00.828 --> 12:03.531
That's my little girl.

12:03.565 --> 12:06.636
Oh, my!

12:12.744 --> 12:14.813
Come in.

12:14.847 --> 12:16.415
Who the hell are you?

12:16.450 --> 12:18.118
Why, your grandma,
of course.

12:18.152 --> 12:19.186
All right, fine.

12:19.220 --> 12:20.320
I guess we're doing this.

12:20.355 --> 12:22.992
My, what big eyes
you have, Grandma.

12:23.026 --> 12:25.528
All the better
to see you with, my dear.

12:25.563 --> 12:27.130
My, what big...
You know what?

12:27.164 --> 12:28.398
I-I'm sorry, I-I can't.

12:28.432 --> 12:30.769
I-I can't do this.
I-I'm not an idiot.

12:30.803 --> 12:32.371
My grandma is a human woman.

12:32.405 --> 12:34.040
How-how was this ever a scene?

12:34.074 --> 12:35.276
All right, fine, yes.

12:35.310 --> 12:36.377
It's me, the wolf.

12:36.411 --> 12:37.913
Must we go through
this charade?

12:37.947 --> 12:39.147
It's insulting.

12:39.181 --> 12:40.448
I don't know
why you're complaining.

12:40.483 --> 12:41.583
I'm the one who's about

12:41.617 --> 12:43.686
to get violently bisected
by the woodsman.

12:43.720 --> 12:45.421
What woodsman?

12:58.875 --> 13:01.044
You know, I'm not sure
if that's our hero

13:01.078 --> 13:02.279
or just a lunatic

13:02.314 --> 13:03.981
going house to house
murdering people.

13:09.756 --> 13:11.191
Yeah, he-he-he
just did it again.

13:11.225 --> 13:12.426
I think we should...

13:12.460 --> 13:14.529
I think we should call somebody.

13:20.849 --> 13:23.084
Aw, look at the little guy.

13:23.119 --> 13:25.020
So peaceful.

13:25.055 --> 13:26.523
Hey! Wake up! We got one more!

13:27.959 --> 13:30.762
Now, if this don't get you
to sleep, nothing will.

13:30.797 --> 13:33.732
"Cinderella"
by nobody remembers.

13:36.104 --> 13:39.007
<i>A long time ago,
in a magical, faraway land,</i>

13:39.041 --> 13:42.410
<i>several women lived together
and, surprise, surprise,</i>

13:42.445 --> 13:44.547
<i>they didn't exactly get along.</i>

13:46.885 --> 13:49.554
Hey, Cinderella,
how's the scrubbing going?

13:49.588 --> 13:52.291
God, we have so few female
characters to work with.

13:52.325 --> 13:54.194
You just keep scrubbing
that poo spot

13:54.228 --> 13:56.464
so I can come back
and poo on that spot again.

13:56.498 --> 13:59.434
You guys are gonna regret
being mean to me someday.

13:59.469 --> 14:01.037
Mean to you? Us?

14:01.071 --> 14:03.607
When are we ever
mean to you?

14:03.642 --> 14:05.509
Remember the time
you told King Midas

14:05.544 --> 14:07.213
to go to third base with me?

14:07.247 --> 14:08.981
Now I'm dealing with this.

14:10.483 --> 14:12.486
I dated him, too.

14:19.163 --> 14:22.199
It's so unfair that we're called
the "evil" stepsisters.

14:22.233 --> 14:24.269
Yeah, I mean,
you'd be evil, too,

14:24.304 --> 14:26.205
if your stepdad was
Bruce Jenner.

14:26.239 --> 14:29.475
Hey, girls, feel my cheek,
it's like a bottom!

14:31.747 --> 14:33.481
He stole me horn!

14:36.821 --> 14:38.655
Well, I don't,
I don't know what that was,

14:38.690 --> 14:41.024
but th-the first one has
a parchment from the Charmings.

14:43.363 --> 14:45.531
It's an invite to a party
for the prince!

14:45.565 --> 14:47.032
I hear he's looking
for someone

14:47.067 --> 14:48.369
to spend the rest
of his life with.

14:48.403 --> 14:49.837
Well, it won't be you.

14:49.871 --> 14:52.741
Yeah, there's a reason this
story's not called "Cinderella."

14:52.775 --> 14:54.142
Actually, it is.

14:54.177 --> 14:57.081
Ah, that does not
bode well for us.

15:01.455 --> 15:03.489
Now, since we're all
planning on drinking,

15:03.523 --> 15:05.592
I called us a pumpkin.

15:05.627 --> 15:06.761
Wait for me!

15:10.432 --> 15:12.501
You said if I had
a nice dress,

15:12.535 --> 15:14.037
I could go to the ball.

15:14.071 --> 15:16.274
How did you even make
that dress so fast?

15:16.308 --> 15:18.709
Oh, you know,
I-I have an eye for fashion,

15:18.744 --> 15:20.880
and I'm pretty good
with my hands.

15:20.914 --> 15:22.248
Unbelievable.

15:22.283 --> 15:24.551
Now I'm worried about that
screenplay we gave her.

15:24.586 --> 15:26.187
You're not going
to the ball!

15:26.222 --> 15:29.158
It's for ladies,
not scumbag nobodies.

15:29.192 --> 15:32.630
Girls, shred her dress and
divvy it up for monthlies.

15:46.482 --> 15:48.351
Well, that's
not cool, either.

15:48.385 --> 15:49.953
They're all kind of bitches.

15:53.993 --> 15:57.364
And then they ripped up my dress
so now I have nothing to wear.

15:57.398 --> 16:00.468
Well, sometimes
"nothing to wear" is a fun time.

16:00.502 --> 16:02.504
You know, just get weird.

16:04.675 --> 16:07.745
Cinderella, I am
your fairy godmother.

16:07.779 --> 16:11.449
"Fairy" in the magical sense,
not about kissing guys.

16:11.483 --> 16:13.085
Oh, my God!

16:13.119 --> 16:16.222
I want that bitch Snow White to
just admit she had an abortion.

16:16.256 --> 16:17.424
Whoa, whoa!

16:17.459 --> 16:19.961
I was thinking more like
a new dress for the party.

16:19.995 --> 16:21.597
Or a bunch of chew toys.

16:21.631 --> 16:22.732
Your choice.

16:22.766 --> 16:24.133
Chew toys.
Take the chew toys.

16:24.167 --> 16:25.469
A new dress?

16:25.503 --> 16:27.705
Well, that means I
could go to the ball!

16:32.480 --> 16:34.815
Oh, what a beautiful dress.

16:34.850 --> 16:36.617
B-But how will I
get to the ball?

16:36.651 --> 16:38.854
I-I don't have a horse
or a carriage.

16:44.997 --> 16:47.599
Oh, yeah, that's... yeah,
just change me into whatever.

16:47.633 --> 16:49.201
Yeah, that's cool. Thanks.

16:49.236 --> 16:50.904
Well, is everything
all right in here...?

16:50.938 --> 16:54.342
This hurts! This hurts!

17:04.123 --> 17:05.691
This ball is kind of lame.

17:05.726 --> 17:08.494
All these royal types
are inbreeding, walleyed,

17:08.529 --> 17:10.798
bucktooth monsters
who have to be wheeled around

17:10.832 --> 17:11.932
under a blanket.

17:11.966 --> 17:14.870
I say! Wherever is Grandmum-mum?

17:14.905 --> 17:18.074
She would so enjoy
the festoonities!

17:18.109 --> 17:19.509
That's not a word, sir.

17:19.544 --> 17:22.614
My mind races from the damp!

17:22.649 --> 17:23.949
Hey, how are you?

17:23.983 --> 17:25.952
Hey, hi, there.
Thanks for coming.

17:25.986 --> 17:29.223
These are my daughters,
and they will do anything

17:29.257 --> 17:32.227
to be your princess,
right, girls?

17:32.261 --> 17:33.797
See anything
you like?

17:33.832 --> 17:36.233
Oh, I'm so fancy
and moist.

17:36.267 --> 17:37.634
Ew, you guys are gross.

17:37.669 --> 17:40.138
But stick around in case
I don't find anyone else.

17:46.114 --> 17:49.217
Okay, first of all,
obviously the dress.

17:50.620 --> 17:52.622
And you smell slightly
less worse

17:52.656 --> 17:54.492
than everyone else
in the kingdom.

17:54.526 --> 17:57.062
Oh, why, thank you,
I just bathed last year.

18:22.365 --> 18:23.632
Hey, wh-where you going?

18:23.666 --> 18:24.666
Come back here!

18:24.700 --> 18:26.001
You brushed up against it!

18:26.035 --> 18:27.771
You got to take care of it now!

18:37.217 --> 18:39.754
Wait, wait, you forgot
your glass slipper.

18:43.092 --> 18:44.326
And a box of condoms.

18:44.360 --> 18:47.231
Aw, man!
Things were gonna happen.

18:53.440 --> 18:55.409
We almost kissed.

18:55.443 --> 18:57.779
Why couldn't the magic have
lasted five more minutes?

18:57.813 --> 19:00.916
Now I'll never get to be
a rich, do-nothing wife.

19:00.951 --> 19:04.221
Sorry your dreams
haven't come true.

19:11.165 --> 19:13.900
My lord, there is no sign
of her, and we searched far.

19:13.934 --> 19:15.804
Did you search wide?
No.

19:15.838 --> 19:18.039
You got to search wide,
that's like half of it.

19:20.444 --> 19:22.679
<i>And so the prince searched
all over the kingdom</i>

19:22.714 --> 19:24.315
<i>for the foot
that fit the glass slipper.</i>

19:24.350 --> 19:25.583
<i>Well, not "all" over.</i>

19:25.618 --> 19:28.822
<i>He skipped the, uh,
south side of town,</i>

19:28.856 --> 19:30.590
<i>which, uh, even
in fairy tale times,</i>

19:30.625 --> 19:32.460
<i>was, um...</i>

19:32.494 --> 19:34.529
<i>let's just say "loud."</i>

19:38.534 --> 19:41.672
And so, whoever fits in this
slipper will be my princess.

19:41.706 --> 19:43.508
Or prince.

19:43.542 --> 19:45.210
I'm bi.

19:45.244 --> 19:47.247
Oh, there's my slipper!

19:47.281 --> 19:48.761
Oh, I've been looking
all over for it.

19:48.783 --> 19:51.486
Well, when I'm not
doing gymnastics.

19:51.520 --> 19:53.489
This could be your life.

19:53.523 --> 19:55.190
Enough!

19:57.361 --> 19:58.696
It's you.

19:58.730 --> 19:59.998
Her?

20:10.746 --> 20:13.516
I can't wait to make love
to you a hundred years

20:13.550 --> 20:16.921
before the invention
of toilet paper.

20:16.955 --> 20:19.858
<i>And so, two people who danced
together one time</i>

20:19.893 --> 20:22.862
<i>entered into an ill-advised,
long-term relationship.</i>

20:22.897 --> 20:25.766
<i>And they lived happily ever
after for seven months</i>

20:25.801 --> 20:28.470
<i>and then separated with
the goal of fixing themselves</i>

20:28.504 --> 20:29.872
<i>and getting back together.</i>

20:29.907 --> 20:32.009
<i>They got into a huge fight
when his mom got sick.</i>

20:32.043 --> 20:34.211
<i>And now they don't even follow
each other on Twitter.</i>

20:34.245 --> 20:35.847
<i>The end.</i>

20:42.724 --> 20:45.960
Good night, Stewie.

20:45.994 --> 20:48.531
Good night, Chris.

20:50.000 --> 20:52.001
Good night, Meg.

20:52.002 --> 21:53.002
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru